## =============================================================================
## Test Suite Overview
## =============================================================================

test:VlmWorkflowStreams
    rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Local VLM workflow streams" ;
    skos:broader test:TestSuite ;
    kpred:description "Run several independent visual analysis streams against a local branch preview. A scripted stream follows configured goto, click and fill steps. An exploratory stream asks a local vision model to choose a visible control, type, scroll, press a key or finish. Each checkpoint runs separate configured analysis lenses, such as layout, readability and progress, with the preceding screenshot available for comparison. Streams run sequentially to avoid competing for GPU memory." ;
    kpred:command "Start a preview, then OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434 npm run visual:streams -- --base=http://localhost:4173. Use --list to validate and list examples, --streams=find-review to select, --model=qwen2.5vl:7b to override models, and --config=path/to/streams.json for custom workflows. scripts/visual-streams/examples.json is the executable contract example." ;
    kpred:description "The JSON version is 1. Each stream has a unique id, mode, goal, startPath and nonempty lenses (id and question). Optional model, viewport, mobile, timeoutMs and maxSteps bound a run. Scripted streams require steps; exploratory streams use screenshot-grounded actions instead. Optional assertions check an exact path or a visible unique selector, with optional contained text. Selector assertions check rendered browser state; they cannot prove a database write unless the workflow exposes that outcome." ;
    kpred:description "Each stream uses fresh browser storage, synthetic UI inputs and an explicit loopback app origin. Network requests are limited to same-origin GET/HEAD; service workers, websocket connections, popups and downloads are unavailable. Real external integrations are outside this harness. Artifacts are private under XDG_STATE_HOME/reckons/visual-streams (default ~/.local/state), with ordered screenshots and hashes, configuration, raw model responses, validated actions, browser errors and assertion results. Run provenance records the checkout commit and dirty flag; it does not attest which build the supplied preview serves." ;
    kpred:honest-note "A verified goal means configured browser assertions passed, not that the VLM's visual judgment is correct. Goal-driven exploration stops when all assertions hold. Without assertions, a model finish is unverified. Step exhaustion, malformed output, deadline and browser failures are incomplete/error results. Visual issues and uncertainty become proposals in the main workspace review queue. CLI exit 2 means failed/incomplete execution, exit 1 means visual proposals need review, exit 0 means the run completed; read each stream status. No cloud fallback and no product edits. This is a local tool, not an autonomous CI approval gate." ;
    kpred:tested-by "scripts/visual-streams/__tests__/contract.test.ts" ;
    kpred:tested-by "tests/e2e/visual-streams.test.ts" .

test:TestSuite
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "Test Suite" ;
    hnav:order          110 ;
    skos:definition     "Reckons.AI test infrastructure: 336+ unit tests (Vitest + jsdom), Playwright E2E with 6 device profiles, visual regression with pixel analysis + DOM overlap + text presence checks, optional Mistral OCR and Claude Vision tiers. All tests run locally without API keys." ;
    skos:related        guide:WhatIsReckonsAI .

test:GraphReviewStory
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "Reckons.AI Graph Review — Goal & Workflow" ;
    <urn:reckons:nav/order> "111"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:definition     """The Reckons.AI Graph Review is an offline, exhaustive audit of the whole app treated as a graph: every button is clicked, every screen is visually checked, and every finding is tied back to the graph for human review. It runs locally and Opus-reviewed — no cloud dependency — and scores against the Web/Mobile UI-UX rubric.

### The goal

Catch the failures a "click everything, flag crashes" pass misses — silent no-ops (a control that fires, throws nothing, and does nothing) and stale-cache regressions — while producing a reviewable, graph-native record rather than a throwaway log.

### Workflow overview

1. **Enumerate** — collect every interactive element on every route (buttons, tabs, leap badges, sheets).
2. **Act and assert a delta** — click each, then check that something observable actually changed (URL, node count, graph id, open panels, title, visible text). This is what catches silent no-ops.
3. **Visual check** — pixel, DOM-overlap and touch-target checks run locally; a local VLM scores each screenshot against the rubric.
4. **Persistent-context pass** — replay against a warm service worker to surface stale-cache regressions that fresh runs never reproduce.
5. **Tie to the graph** — each route becomes a TestWorkflow and each click a TestStep, carrying its screenshot, a pass/fail verdict, and a citation to any rubric guideline it violates; findings queue as pending facts for review.
6. **Review and grow** — Opus reads the coverage gaps and authors new predetermined paths, so the library grows over time.

This page is the goal and workflow overview; the stepped review itself is generated as a TestWorkflow story.""" ;
    skos:broader        test:TestSuite .


## =============================================================================
## Story: Reckons.AI Graph Review
## =============================================================================
## The stepped, in-app story for the offline exhaustive graph review — grounded
## in the "Goal & Workflow" overview (test:GraphReviewStory). Steps 1–4 carry
## real screenshots captured while driving the app; each step names the delta it
## asserts, so the story shows WHY a crash-only crawl is not enough.

test:GraphReviewFlow
    rdf:type            story:Story ;
    rdfs:label          "Reckons.AI Graph Review" ;
    story:description   "Walk the offline exhaustive graph review as it runs against the app: enumerate every control, click each, and assert an observable delta so silent no-ops are caught — then tie every finding back to the graph for review." ;
    story:autoplay      "false" ;
    story:pace          "10" ;
    kpred:screenshot-dir "tests/visual/screenshots/graph-review/" ;
    skos:broader        test:GraphReviewStory .

test:GraphReview-Step1
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:GraphReviewFlow ;
    story:order         "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Enumerate every control" ;
    story:content       "The review starts on the landing route and enumerates every interactive element — buttons, tabs, leap badges, sheets. The landing page alone exposes 18 controls; the crawl repeats this per route." ;
    story:highlight     test:GraphReviewStory ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/graph-review/01-enumerate-landing.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "interactive element count > 0" ;
    kpred:page          "/" .

test:GraphReview-Step2
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:GraphReviewFlow ;
    story:order         "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Act and assert a delta" ;
    story:content       "Click the hero 'Getting started' button and assert the docs graph actually activates — 119 nodes laid out, not a silent no-op. A click that fires without changing anything observable is a finding." ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/graph-review/02-getting-started-graph.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "node-label count > 0 after click" ;
    kpred:page          "/" .

test:GraphReview-Step3
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:GraphReviewFlow ;
    story:order         "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Catch the silent no-op" ;
    story:content       "Follow a graph leap and assert the graph swapped to the target sub-graph — currentKbId changed and 39 new nodes rendered. This is the exact silent-no-op class a crash-only crawler misses (the docs-hub leap regression fixed this session)." ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/graph-review/03-leap-jump-subgraph.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "currentKbId changed after leap" ;
    kpred:page          "/" .

test:GraphReview-Step4
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:GraphReviewFlow ;
    story:order         "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Visual check, locally" ;
    story:content       "On each screen run the offline pixel, DOM-overlap and touch-target checks — no blank/solid-fill, targets at least 44px — before any VLM scoring. Cheapest checks first, no API keys." ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/graph-review/04-review-visual-check.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "pixel.isSolidFill === false" ;
    kpred:page          "/review" .

test:GraphReview-Step5
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:GraphReviewFlow ;
    story:order         "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Tie every finding to the graph" ;
    story:content       "Each route becomes a TestWorkflow and each click a TestStep carrying its screenshot, a pass/fail verdict, and a citation to any rubric guideline it violates; the worst findings queue as pending facts for human review." ;
    kpred:assertion     "findings queued to knowledge.pending.jsonl" ;
    kpred:page          "/review" .

test:GraphReview-Step6
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:GraphReviewFlow ;
    story:order         "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Review and grow" ;
    story:content       "Opus reads the coverage gaps and authors new predetermined paths, so the story library grows over time — the 'living coverage' in F34." ;
    story:highlight     test:GraphReviewStory ;
    kpred:page          "/review" .

test:UnitTests
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "Unit Tests" ;
    skos:definition     "336+ tests via Vitest with jsdom environment. Coverage: RDF serialize/import, temporal conflict detection, semantic diff, merge analysis, content safety (28 tests), embedding, mobile auth. Run: npx vitest run." ;
    kpred:test-count    "336" ;
    kpred:framework     "vitest" ;
    kpred:command       "npx vitest run" ;
    skos:broader        test:TestSuite .

test:VisualTests
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "Visual Regression Tests" ;
    skos:definition     "Playwright-based visual regression. 5 analysis layers (cheapest first): pixel analysis (solid fill, color anomaly), DOM overlap detection, text presence checks, Mistral OCR (if API key), Claude Vision semantic analysis (if API key). Screenshots saved to tests/visual/screenshots/." ;
    kpred:framework     "playwright" ;
    kpred:command       "npm run test:visual" ;
    skos:broader        test:TestSuite .

test:UserStoryTests
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "User Story Tests" ;
    skos:definition     "End-to-end test scenarios that follow real user workflows. Each story imports graphs, navigates pages, takes screenshots at each step, and verifies UI state. Three stories: Dev Sprint Planning, User Docs Import, Cross-Graph Alignment." ;
    kpred:command       "npm run test:stories" ;
    skos:broader        test:VisualTests .


## =============================================================================
## Story: Developer Sprint Planning
## =============================================================================
## This is a real Playwright test (tests/visual/user-stories/dev-sprint.test.ts)
## captured as a Story. Each step has an order, description, screenshot path,
## and the assertions it verifies.

test:DevSprintStory
    rdf:type            story:Story ;
    rdfs:label          "Developer Sprint Planning" ;
    story:description   "A developer uses the Production and Roadmap graphs to plan a sprint. They import both graphs, compare them on the graph page, navigate to the align tab, run alignment, and verify the suggestions render correctly." ;
    story:autoplay      "false" ;
    story:pace          "10" ;
    kpred:test-file     "tests/visual/user-stories/dev-sprint.test.ts" ;
    kpred:screenshot-dir "tests/visual/screenshots/dev-sprint/" ;
    skos:broader        test:UserStoryTests .

test:DevSprint-Step1
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Import Production graph" ;
    story:content       "Clear all graphs, then import the Production Status graph. Navigate to the main page. Verify the graph renders (not a solid fill). The Production graph contains test suite entities, architecture components, and MCP tools." ;
    story:highlight     test:UnitTests ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/dev-sprint/01-production-imported.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "pixel.isSolidFill === false" ;
    kpred:page          "/" .

test:DevSprint-Step2
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Import Roadmap graph" ;
    story:content       "Import the Roadmap graph alongside the Production graph. Both graphs now coexist. The roadmap contains planned features with statuses (done, in-progress, planned)." ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/dev-sprint/02-roadmap-imported.png" ;
    kpred:page          "/" .

test:DevSprint-Step3
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Graph Page Shows Both graphs" ;
    story:content       "Navigate to /kb. Both imported graphs appear in the registry list. Select two graphs for comparison using the compare checkboxes." ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/dev-sprint/03-kb-page-both.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "Graph entry count >= 2" ;
    kpred:page          "/kb" .

test:DevSprint-Step4
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Align Link Appears" ;
    story:content       "After selecting two graphs for comparison, an 'align these graphs' link appears. This link navigates to the Review page with the align tab pre-selected." ;
    kpred:assertion     "align link is visible" ;
    kpred:page          "/kb" .

test:DevSprint-Step5
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Review Align Tab with graph Picker" ;
    story:content       "Navigate to /review and switch to the align tab. The graph picker component renders with chips for each available graph. Select a source graph to align against the active graph." ;
    kpred:assertion     "Graph picker chip count >= 1" ;
    kpred:page          "/review?tab=align" .

test:DevSprint-Step6
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Run Alignment" ;
    story:content       "Click the first graph chip, then click the align button. Wait for alignment to complete (entity matching via exact IRI + embedding similarity). Results appear as AlignmentCards showing source→target entity matches." ;
    kpred:assertion     "alignment results render" ;
    kpred:page          "/review?tab=align" .

test:DevSprint-Step7
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "7"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "Summary Chips Render" ;
    story:content       "After alignment, summary chips show the breakdown: add (new entities), reinforce (matching entities), conflict (contradictions). These chips use the same diff categories as the incoming tab." ;
    kpred:assertion     "summary chips include add/reinforce/conflict" ;
    kpred:page          "/review?tab=align" .

test:DevSprint-Step8
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "AlignmentCard Shows Flow" ;
    story:content       "Each AlignmentCard shows the source→target graph entity flow with accept and reject buttons. The developer can approve matches (remapping the entity IRI) or reject them (keeping separate entities)." ;
    kpred:assertion     "ac-flow, ac-accept, ac-reject visible" ;
    kpred:page          "/review?tab=align" .

test:DevSprint-Step9
    rdf:type            story:Step ;
    story:partOf        test:DevSprintStory ;
    story:order         "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    story:title         "No Rendering Artifacts" ;
    story:content       "Final check: the review page renders without solid fills, color anomalies, or visual artifacts. This validates the entire flow completed without rendering errors." ;
    kpred:icon2d        "/tests/visual/screenshots/dev-sprint/09-no-artifacts.png" ;
    kpred:assertion     "pixel.isSolidFill === false, pixel.hasColorAnomaly === false" ;
    kpred:page          "/review" .


