## --- Run summary written back as data (F183.2): the measured claim lives beside the task it measured ---

bench:Result-image-2026-10-14 rdf:type bench:RunSummary ;
    rdfs:label "Image bench run, hard tier, 2026-10-14" ;
    skos:broader bench:Task-image ;
    bench:run-date "2026-10-14" ;
    bench:tier "hard" ;
    bench:judge "qwen2.5vl:7b" ;
    bench:arm "incumbent: Z-Image-Turbo Q8_0 (Apache-2.0), quality 0.913, 14.0 s/run, peak 11992 MiB, 30 of 30 hard checks" ;
    bench:arm "candidate: vnbot-ai/Z-Image-Turbo-GGUF Q4_K_M (apache-2.0), quality 0.907, 16.5 s/run, peak 10503 MiB, 30 of 30 hard checks" ;
    bench:incumbent-seed-spread "0.060" ;
    bench:quality-delta "-0.007" ;
    bench:verdict "hold" ;
    kpred:description "10 hard briefs x 3 seeds x 2 arms = 60 images, judged item by item. The verdict is hold, not insufficient-evidence: the incumbent mean 0.913 is under the 0.95 ceiling, so the ceiling rule did not trigger. The arms do not separate (delta -0.007 against an incumbent seed spread of 0.060). The briefs now have headroom: counts and a spatial scene vary (five-apples 0.4 to 1.0, four-ducks 0.6 to 1.0), but 6 of 10 briefs are still perfect for both arms. The judge is a 7B vision model whose answers on counts are themselves uncertain; none of its answers were checked by a human." .

test:ThreeExampleNodes rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Three.js example loading and isolation" ;
    skos:broader test:TestSuite ;
    skos:definition "Attach a synthetic official-host WebGL example through node details. Before Load, there is no remote request or iframe. After a real WebGL draw, the viewer reports running. Verify parent-document and storage isolation, CSP network restrictions after document replacement, top-navigation denial, Stop/remove, HTTP and script errors, context loss, unsupported graphics APIs, a render deadline, forged-message refusal and a missing heartbeat. Desktop and phone Chromium use deterministic intercepted upstream responses, including the production SAMEORIGIN frame header." ;
    kpred:command "npx playwright test tests/e2e/three-example.test.ts --project=desktop-chrome --project=mobile-android" ;
    kpred:honest-note "Fixtures verify the viewer boundary, not compatibility with every changing upstream example. An iframe does not guarantee containment of GPU-driver or browser-process crashes. WebGPU-specific device behavior needs a compatible device; the deterministic scene uses WebGL2." ;
    kpred:tested-by "tests/e2e/three-example.test.ts", "src/lib/3d/__tests__/three-example.test.ts" .
